     takes input — but it IS selectable and reachable, so the ring stays on keyboard focus and only
     the hover treatment goes. */
  .rep-end__url:hover {
    border-color: var(--bo-base-300);
  }

  /* ── THE COPY BUTTON AND ITS ONE STATE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Two labels in one grid cell, so the box is as wide as the wider word and a press cannot resize
     it. Oleh asked for the confirmation to *"turn green and fade out"*, and the fade is the whole
     reason the colour goes on a transition rather than being swapped: green arriving instantly and
     leaving slowly is what makes it read as an acknowledgement rather than as a second button. */
  .rep-end__copy {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    transition:
      color 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
      border-color 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

